  "source": "Mixamo Static Double Dagger Stab With Outward Grip, motion id c9c69305-b96c-11e4-a802-0aaa78deedf9, frames 1-93",
  "fix": "Derek's Unity pass on a5a5dd1d: hands look ok, but both blades point off to his side. The fists were aimed along the hips bone's local Z. At rest that axis is the face, but during this clip it yaws off the fight's forward. The fight's forward is Blender -Y. FBX axis_forward=-Z axis_up=Y maps that to Unity model +Z, and NewCharsPreview turns model +Z onto world +X with Quaternion.LookRotation(Vector3.right). Kaelen stands at x=-1.7 and Vorgath is at x=+2.3 on the same lane, so +X is toward the enemy. Both forearms and hands now point along that axis, with the same straight fist (blade out the front of the hand, wrist aligned with the forearm). On content frames 12-24 the right arm is lifted, and on 12-18 it is yawed up to 15 degrees outward, so the blade stays in front of the chest instead of passing through it. Idle, walk, dualslash, and the shared slash props are unchanged.",
  "unity_change": "None. HoldGrips still applies KAELEN_sword_L_stab.fbx / KAELEN_sword_R_stab.fbx only while the clip is attack2_crossthrust. Those stab props and the shared KAELEN_sword_L.fbx / KAELEN_sword_R.fbx are unchanged. The new heading is in the attack2 forearm and hand curves.",
